## CONTEXT BAND AND HANDOVER
At about 70% context, start no new step. At about 75%, stop at a safe boundary: files whole, every process you started stopped by pid, the lock released, `head` clean. Write `/Volumes/Datasec_DEV/!CODING/Datasec/HPSM-POC/1_Project_Definition/Briefs/2026-11-17_B1672_HANDOVER.md` (done / in hand / next / processes left / decisions a successor keeps: the base sha, the target version, the per-shard table so far). Its last line is `HANDOVER B1672: next step <n> | done steps <list>`; end STATUS with the same line. The e2e of eight shards is the long part: after each shard write its row to STATUS so a successor never repeats one.

## HARD STOP (slot)
At the HARD STOP clock of the Stamp: start nothing new, push nothing unproven. A committed but unpushed head is `CODED-UNPROVEN <branch> <sha40>` in STATUS with the steps that ran. Write the HANDOVER and end on its line.

